:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467546} {:answer/id #uuid "a49d1e0b-d87d-5990-9f1d-19472bb6081c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467547} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5dbf19f-117b-5de5-8d38-1828f362ece6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468494}] :question/id #uuid "7f48e886-80d4-5268-94be-6547f7232323" :question/math-academy-id "q-42957" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 10 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n- **I.** $A$ has identical columns\n- **II.** $A$ has a zero column\n- **III.** $A$ has identical rows\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\n- $A$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 10 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ has identical rows: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 10 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351410 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87131d2a-00fa-5c86-adb5-5dcd9781663d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451839} {:answer/id #uuid "c5992e5f-0eac-5510-8b9e-4c9bdb590e1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451840} :answer-field/id #uuid "f556a776-7b3e-5b87-96a3-38f6c6a85224" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452767} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94e1abfb-4ac1-5387-8365-44f8be67855e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451841} {:answer/id #uuid "1ae75960-5f9e-5be6-9aa4-ca852b78c6e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451841} :answer-field/id #uuid "4203a946-5791-54e5-8948-df9e4bceec16" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452768} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3316e667-7cb8-5d37-8ca1-05b94216632d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451843} {:answer/id #uuid "e4ec2c90-b24e-58ba-a3ab-9443e572892a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451843} :answer-field/id #uuid "038959f0-30da-57d8-900b-1c0a7eef35de" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452769}] :question/id #uuid "e8066ca0-5e8f-5876-924e-8be55bf1f74e" :question/math-academy-id "q-82290" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** One of the rows/columns of $A$ is proportional to another row/column of $A$\n- **II.** $A$ has two identical rows\n- **III.** $A$ has a zero row" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nIn the case of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, this means that one of the rows/columns must be proportional to another row/column.\n\n- Statements II and III are false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWe have that \n\n$$\n|A|=4\\cdot 3-6\\cdot 2=0\n$$\n\nbut $A$ has neither two identical rows nor a zero row.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415476 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "071ee791-8aa1-59a9-829e-f23787b55570" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473130} {:answer/id #uuid "be789ad4-7b1c-517c-b647-7e02fbdc4606" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473131} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c846e82-5642-55c2-bd6c-bf9a65cc14b7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473960} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "380f5ebb-1b0a-524b-8107-7d50c50a8d0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473132} {:answer/id #uuid "2adc7349-dd06-5e86-bb35-5bbbb5b04583" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473132} :answer-field/id #uuid "37aa9389-4822-5c22-ad9b-bf758d46df45" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473961} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2322edf-ee14-5f20-8831-ec7cadfc1dd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473134} {:answer/id #uuid "d8ca5be3-1fbc-5f41-bcbb-41b53ef5da56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473135} :answer-field/id #uuid "873d7824-ac7f-5ce0-ad45-49263a39fd15" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473962}] :question/id #uuid "8d883981-f066-5218-a1bf-dd76574de46e" :question/math-academy-id "q-42469" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2.05 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{7} & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n- **I.** $A$ has proportional columns\n- **II.** $A$ has identical rows\n- **III.** $A$ has a zero row\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2.05 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{7} & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical rows.\n\n- $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2.05 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{7} & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415479 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c54ada56-3e8b-562f-84dd-634b27dac9cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453904} {:answer/id #uuid "1bc835ea-e9b6-5ca5-a77e-0c3bd1af050b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453904} :answer-field/id #uuid "63c0a961-3dd4-5dcd-85e3-43b3a0493c55" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454702} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2456bbca-5dde-5fa3-a774-4b5dfb8431ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453906} {:answer/id #uuid "1b80c1f5-4c11-5a34-bb1a-faf5cdfce42f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453906} :answer-field/id #uuid "36456e08-b5e0-5ffb-8bc0-2e13784267ad" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454703} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e336f47-61c7-5dfa-b071-bc593d519e33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453908} {:answer/id #uuid "05d59b93-9de5-5bdc-af50-0154b6214595" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453909} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bb3bd4f-a1b2-5b23-a316-a0c1d1cd0bc3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454704}] :question/id #uuid "f8a11ae3-b740-5975-a251-a4796d69b742" :question/math-academy-id "q-43307" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $3\\times 3$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ has a zero column\n- **II.** $A$ has two proportional rows\n- **III.** One of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nExpending across the $1$st column, we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(3-2)+(1-2) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbut $A$ has neither a zero column nor two proportional rows.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420353 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8345ca2e-07d0-5694-85e8-8ac1bcfa3d94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474822} {:answer/id #uuid "b5ff36f5-8430-54a9-bec5-2cc165a0f1ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474822} :answer-field/id #uuid "df50f4aa-1524-57d2-b1e7-0affdd885093" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475337} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "902e3414-ca2a-5ce2-850b-da2dc63be023" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474824} {:answer/id #uuid "4e173f75-196d-539f-971b-b9d002b2252d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474824} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4a68604-a5fe-5780-aff3-ee5e03c398ad" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475338} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c276a60-9989-5c94-9ab0-70747f4dd816" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474826} {:answer/id #uuid "50bacac0-c323-5e20-9449-31c6507754e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474827} :answer-field/id #uuid "affe140d-4863-54d4-bd0d-1629fd85f31c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475339}] :question/id #uuid "d2486be8-75b8-51f1-882e-08f8a79961f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-42463" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n- **I.** $A$ has identical rows\n- **II.** $A$ has proportional columns\n- **III.** $A$ has a zero row\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical rows.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have proportional columns.\n\n- $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :topic/math-academy-id 2201 :topic/title "Conditions When a Determinant Equals Zero"}] [{:activity/_scope [{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120724} :activity/id #uuid "e15d96c3-59f3-5ea3-8c30-d6c68ac605ad" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120724 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186121054 :tutorial/content "Suppose we want to find the shortest distance between the point $P(3,0,-2)$ and the plane $\\Pi$ that is given by the equation \n\n$$\n(\\mathbf{r}-\\langle 2 , 3 , 1 \\rangle ) \\cdot \\langle 4 , 4 , 2 \\rangle = 0.\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, note that $\\mathbf{n} = \\langle 4 , 4 , 2 \\rangle$ is a vector that's normal to the plane.\n\n![](images/7b/7b2dfcd87c1f5e4e2c2b1a0b9a7f73899772e33e1020465b2b38d1b2de29a66c.png)\n\nLet's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(2,3,1)$. Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,3,1⟩-⟨3,0,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,3,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe shortest distance $d$ from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/26/26e494eef47db4dba3ac36dfa96c7e9a9d191321b22bb82874f3e74bbd7116ef.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot 4+3\\cdot 4+3\\cdot 2|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-4+12+6|}{\\sqrt{16+16+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|14|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is $\\dfrac{7}{3}.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "224c4104-9097-5a92-9c37-5d0fe22171a6" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3261 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "9e02b271-c1ce-518a-b549-4e83a2061ea7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120725}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120725 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119839 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7"} :step/id #uuid "3779ed6b-358c-5101-8bd7-9de56abc2ade" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120726}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120726 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119840 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d"} :step/id #uuid "213ff9e2-fe7a-528b-b535-4cf580c6aca9" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120727}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120727 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119841 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f"} :step/id #uuid "fdb4920a-a24d-544c-bdef-93ed800bfdd9"}] :activity/title "The Shortest Distance Between a Plane and a Point" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186120020} {:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186477001} :activity/id #uuid "607e9414-4918-5745