answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291626} :answer-field/id #uuid "d58c800e-db81-5f5d-a314-1fbbd43f6acc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292382}] :question/id #uuid "9afdc46e-e890-5eab-ac3f-a6908140cd13" :question/math-academy-id "q-275984" :question/problem "![](images/32/32fc2965c35872f2511ab7c24e931d62c8cbcc6d1c70c67cad6016dedad5d8fd.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=2\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=0\\cdot 3-(-1)\\cdot 2=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,2\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297501 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0b7ecc1-e9b8-5b8b-964c-e4cf9a4249ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "84" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296121}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "84" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296121} :answer-field/id #uuid "d36acde6-4a09-5ef4-9906-e204f2625e8b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297074}] :question/id #uuid "c3acf041-eb7f-5e8e-b449-367