-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 2=3.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 1=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,5\\,|\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297503 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b373104-387f-5698-b1c5-ff0306bfa57b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295793} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbcd2ef4-faa2-5438-a1a2-ee9d6bdc8d72" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297087}] :question/id #uuid "a42863c3-7761-5c90-b6bd-06f39444b587" :question/math-academy-id "q-316584" :question/problem "![](images/f3/f38424364e3d4efd8ebc416974163e3eb87b3350c0c6b8ec7f5ae4ea69339824.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=1\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 2=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,4\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297504 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a72305af-6015-5a67-9a53-61b172148c0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296146} :answer-field/id #uuid "64af5f53-2d9a-5da9-820b-14a837fc2b01" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296841}] :question/id #uuid "b5093505-1cef-57a3-9393-884c4f2f64a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-316585" :question/problem "![](images/7e/7edace8cab645caab8309768ede92f534281567640aba7082f647ca1c8a49074.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=3\\cdot 4=12.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 1=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,3\\,|\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297505 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b8a61de-b029-5aa3-937c-791d1b86aea8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:d