| \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297494 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e046d20a-588d-5b92-a657-b3ed4097c01b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296459} :answer-field/id #uuid "235cb913-9e0f-518e-a93e-a8ac9c3649b3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296695}] :question/id #uuid "b409383e-6fc2-599c-a9ff-f2d3f2066a9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-316567" :question/problem "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\nThe area scale factor is\n{{field-1}} ." :question/worked-solution "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|6\\cdot 3-5\\cdot 4| \\\\  & =|18-20| \\\\  & =|-2| \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297495 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee63275b-2854-5ded-a179-79b5d7d5f1d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "89" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296532}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "89" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296532} :answer-field/id #uuid "642ebee4-29eb-58ed-91c1-e48ef7bc9422" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296839}] :question/id #uuid "4c2b63b5-8e9a-53f8-91df-f96b487d39a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-316569" :question/problem "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 8\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\nThe area scale factor is\n{{field-1}} ." :question/worked-solution "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|-10\\cdot 8-9\\cdot 1| \\\\  & =|-80-9| \\\\  & =|-89| \\\\  & =89.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297496 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1951a6be-1532-5bf0-b953-a8a259d62706" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295416}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295416} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bd1c613-aa0f-579d-8531-78890bdba5ba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296860}] :question/id #uuid "74f25c82-a67d-56cf-b708-a7f7d4c8d54e" :question/math-academy-id "q-316570" :question/problem "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -10 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\nThe area scale factor is\n{{field-1}} ." :question/worked-solution "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|6\\cdot 3-(-10)\\cdot (-5)| \\\\  & =|18-50| \\\\  & =|-32| \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297497 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79a2ffbc-e1ce-5bc2-85a5-d261eaf7d37e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "83" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295932}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "83" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295932} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b6cff15-b6c8-52c0-b19b-c28ec078d77d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296685}] :question/id #uuid "2111fc26-d996-5d1d-a930-d12f9563ae8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-316571" :question/problem "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 10 \\\\ 8 & -1\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\nThe area scale factor is\n{{field-1}} ." :question/worked-solution "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|3\\cdot (-1)-10\\cdot 8| \\\\  & =|-3-80| \\\\  & =|-83| \\\\  & =83.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297498 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "861028d2-4e5b-5441-aba8-939308df93de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295986} :answer-field/id #uuid "273d93cc-fc11-532f-9fec-1702fee2c232" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296706}] :question/id #uuid "d6ed5603-df26-5609-9767-31ff4e7c4552" :question/math-academy-id "q-316573" :question/problem "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -5\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\nThe area scale factor is\n{{field-1}} ." :question/worked-solution "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|-6\\cdot (-5)-1\\cdot (-4)| \\\\  & =|30-(-4)| \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297499 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c240b9cd-6090-54d9-afd2-6f7c1b4e5ccd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296293}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296293} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e6f9b78-f98c-5255-8629-